output.generality:
This is the union of the source changes, each still keyed on general plan properties:
- bloom filters on the first equality key of hash joins, with an exact bitmap when the build key is integral and its range is at most 128 bits per build row;
- range-set zonemap filters for join builds with up to 64× the IN-list threshold of distinct integral keys;
- perfect hash joins for RIGHT joins and for dense key ranges up to 4M;
- large (up to 22-bit) dense perfect hash aggregates with parallel combine and scan;
- the fused and replicated small perfect hash aggregates (q01);
- the q02, q16 and q19 optimizer and storage changes.

None of these apply when the keys are non-integral, there are casts or offsets on the bloom-filter path, the tables are sparse, or memory is tight; those cases fall back to the existing code.
